{"schema_version":"1.7.5","id":"USN-8387-1","published":"2026-06-04T23:16:19Z","modified":"2026-06-08T23:14:21.135553506Z","related":["UBUNTU-CVE-2026-28372","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-32746","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-32772"],"upstream":["CVE-2026-28372","CVE-2026-32746","CVE-2026-32772","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-28372","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-32746","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-32772"],"summary":"inetutils vulnerabilities","details":"It was discovered that the Inetutils telnet daemon incorrectly handled\nthe CREDENTIALS_DIRECTORY environment variable. An attacker could possibly\nuse this issue to escalate privileges. (CVE-2026-28372)\n\nIt was discovered that the Inetutils telnet daemon did not properly\nvalidate buffer bounds when processing LINEMODE SLC suboptions. An attacker\ncould possibly use this issue to cause a denial of service or execute\narbitrary code. (CVE-2026-32746)\n\nIt was discovered that the Inetutils telnet client incorrectly handled the\nNEW_ENVIRON SEND USERVAR option. An attacker could possibly use this issue\nto read arbitrary environment variables. (CVE-2026-32772)","affected":[{"package":{"name":"inetutils","ecosystem":"Ubuntu:Pro:14.04:LTS","purl":"pkg:deb/ubuntu/inetutils?arch=source&distro=esm-infra-legacy%2Ftrusty"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"2:1.9.2-1ubuntu0.1~esm4"}]}],"versions":["2:1.9.1.306-0a482-1","2:1.9.1.363-bbc1-1","2:1.9.2-1","2:1.9.2-1ubuntu0.1~esm1","2:1.9.2-1ubuntu0.1~esm2"],"ecosystem_specific":{"availability":"Available with Ubuntu Pro with Legacy support add-on: https://ubuntu.com/pro","binaries":[{"binary_name":"inetutils-ftp","binary_version":"2:1.9.2-1ubuntu0.1~esm4"},{"binary_name":"inetutils-ftpd","binary_version":"2:1.9.2-1ubuntu0.1~esm4"},{"binary_name":"inetutils-inetd","binary_version":"2:1.9.2-1ubuntu0.1~esm4"},{"binary_name":"inetutils-ping","binary_version":"2:1.9.2-1ubuntu0.1~esm4"},{"binary_name":"inetutils-syslogd","binary_version":"2:1.9.2-1ubuntu0.1~esm4"},{"binary_name":"inetutils-talk","binary_version":"